      "impact": "A comparator can reveal the frozen downstream target plus an unrelated frozen source index, inspect no semantic rule projection, and still produce a structurally valid comparison. This defeats the omission-detection purpose of the mandatory semantic projection across all 140 units.",
      "minimalFix": [
        "Define a closed allowlist for artifacts that can carry semantic-projection and exclude all source-extraction files, *-source-index.json files, source-registry.json, schemas, validators, and other non-projection metadata.",
        "Require at least one actual behavior projection for every comparison; with the current corpus this should include docs/rules/semantics/pilots.json, while questions/conflicts may be additional semantic artifacts.",
        "Add negative controls showing that every frozen source-index path is rejected under semantic-projection and that a real projection still passes."
      ]
    }
